. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
.         
.         * We consider the variable GenderAttitude a suitable measure of suppo
> rt for 
.         * gender equality, where higher values indicate greater support. To e
> stimate 
.         * if having daughters leads to a larger increase in the support of ge
> nder 
.         * equality for men than for women, we conduct an instrumental variabl
> e (IV) 
.         * estimation using linear OLS regression. Specifically, we instrument
>  the 
.         * variable HasDaughter with first_daughter that indicates if the firs
> t born 
.         * child is a daughter and interact if with the variable male_parent t
> hat 
.         * indicates if the respondent is male.
.         
.         gen has_daughter_male = has_daughter*male_parent        
(10,637 missing values generated)

.         gen first_daughter_male = first_daughter*male_parent
(10,637 missing values generated)

.         
.         ivreg2 GenderAttitude male_parent (has_daughter has_daughter_male= fi
> rst_daughter first_daughter_male ) $controls, robust first
